  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...The remnants of the noreaster will impact the \nregion tonight into Tuesday with occasional rain.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nThe vertically stacked noreaster will move to the Gulf of Maine \ntonight while the surface low slowly fills. A weakening band of rain \nto the north of the system is currently lifting across northern \nMaine. Another area of rain will expand across the region \ntonight with the approaching vertically stacked system. This \nsystem will cross the Gulf of Maine Tuesday. This will keep \noccasional rain or showers across the region through Tuesday. \nThe system then begins to exit across the Maritimes Tuesday \nnight, with surface/upper level ridging then starting to build \nacross the region late. Any lingering showers should end \nTuesday evening, leaving partly/mostly cloudy skies overnight. \nAdditional rainfall tonight through Tuesday evening should \ngenerally range from around a quarter to half inch, with locally\nhigher totals possible. We do not expect any flooding concerns \nanywhere given the D1-D3 drought conditions. In fact nearly all \nof the rainfall will likely be absorbed into the near surface \nground and very unlikely any water gets into the rivers and \nstreams. Rivers and streams are currently in the 1-15th \npercentile range with many approaching top 5 lowest flows on \nrecord. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Next round of rain showers expected for the end\nof next week. Drought relief unlikely. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2 DESCRIPTION...\nHigh pressure will build across the region behind current\nNoreaster, bringing dry conditions until late week. Low pressure\nto the northwest in Canada tracks eastward, bringing a \nrelatively weak cold front through the state Thursday night \ninto Friday. Not anticipating heavy rain or high rain totals at \nthis time. Based on global models, PWATs seem to range from \nnormal, to slight above normal. Rain approaches from the NW, \nand exits in the SE. High pressure builds in behind this frontal\nsystem over the weekend.",
